From: programista-zacny <5969291+programista-zacny@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] pidfd: add pidfd_open(), pidfd_send_signal(), exit polling and
 waitid(P_PIDFD)

File descriptors that refer to a process, behind the new option
CONFIG_PIDFD (mainline has none). Android's lmkd opens a pidfd for every
process it may have to kill, kills through it and waits for the death
with epoll; installd, ART and dumpstate wait for their children the same
way.

Mainline commits:
  3eb39f47934f signal: add pidfd_send_signal() syscall (v5.1)
  b3e583825266 clone: add CLONE_PIDFD (v5.2), only the pidfd file and its
               fdinfo
  32fcb426ec00 pid: add pidfd_open() (v5.3)
  b53b0b9d9a61 pidfd: add polling support (v5.3)
  b191d6491be6 pidfd: fix a poll race when setting exit_state
  3695eae5fee0 pidfd: add P_PIDFD to waitid() (v5.4)

The ARM syscall slots reserved by the table extension are wired up: 424
pidfd_send_signal, 434 pidfd_open. Both have cond_syscall() entries, so
with CONFIG_PIDFD off they return -ENOSYS as before.

Adapted to 3.10:
  - The code is in a file of its own, kernel/pidfd.c, instead of being
    spread over pid.c, fork.c and signal.c.
  - No PIDTYPE_TGID: pidfd_open() accepts a pid whose task is a thread
    group leader.
  - Poll wakeup. Mainline wakes the pollers from do_notify_parent() and,
    since b191d6491be6, sets exit_state before that call. 3.10's
    exit_notify() sets exit_state after do_notify_parent(); instead of
    reordering it, the pollers are woken a second time in exit_notify()
    right after exit_state is set. The call in do_notify_parent() covers
    the delayed notification of a leader whose last thread goes away in
    release_task().
  - pidfd_send_signal() only takes pidfds, not /proc/<pid> directory
    descriptors.
  - fdinfo prints "Pid:" in the pid namespace of the reader; a 3.10
    seq_file does not lead back to the procfs instance.
  - struct pid gets the wait queue only with CONFIG_PIDFD.

Not implemented: CLONE_PIDFD, pidfd_getfd(), PIDFD_NONBLOCK, and
process_madvise()/process_mrelease(), which take a pidfd.

[combined set, 2026-11-06] From staging/backport-psi-pidfd
0049, renumbered to 0024 to follow the combined series (0014-0023); it
does not need the PSI/workingset patches 0040-0048 it was written on top
of. Changed in one way: the hunks for arch/arm/include/uapi/asm/unistd.h,
arch/arm/kernel/calls.S and kernel/sys_ni.c (the two __NR_ numbers, the
two table entries and the two cond_syscall() lines) are not in this file
any more. They are in the replacement for patch 0008 of this set,
because they change lines 0008 adds and scripts/prepare-tree.sh
cannot handle that (see the note there). The two files together produce
the same tree as the staged 0049 on top of the canonical 0008. Everything
else is unchanged.

Compile-tested on top of the combined series: zImage with CONFIG_PIDFD=y
and with CONFIG_PIDFD off (GCC 4.9, the Android build's flags), no
warnings in the files touched. Not run on the device.
